  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In Divine Emperor City’s painting world, a market crowd watches a middle-aged man in beast skin clothing put his head into a leopard’s mouth and take it out unharmed. The beast tamer profession had never existed in that painting world before. It appears after the ten children of human path fail to take growling beast painting world and recuperate. Beside hero Gu, scholar Gu, soldier Gu, and craftsman Gu, this Gu shows up in the market.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "house_divine_emperor_city",
          "gu_hero_gu",
          "gu_scholar_gu",
          "gu_craftsman_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Beast tamers specialize in dealing with wild beasts and are more proficient at taming them for their own use. Fang Di Chang finds no specific creator. It appears so naturally that he cannot name a target. He says growling beast painting world will be at a disadvantage now that this Gu has appeared. Shen Shang treats it as one of three kinds of human path Gu worms: a profession Gu, grouped with craftsman Gu and hero Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          2111
        ],
